alsa mailing lists are hosted by sourceforge.net

sourceforge is extraordinarily strict about the configuration of 
your mail host. i had to switch ISP's in order to use sourceforge
email after they tightened things up. many ISPs just don't follow all
the standard (and reasonable) configuration requirements that flow
from SMTP and other standards.

there are many things that your mail host could be failing at. sf.net
has documentation on it, all of which is 100% correct in my
experience.

